**/node_modules
**/dist
backend/static
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/*.log
.git
.github
*.md
# ...but NOT the scaffold template. Its README/ARCHITECTURE/docs/README are
# content the app SHIPS into new repos, not repo documentation — and
# `docs/README.md` carries the tier convention itself. Excluding them would make
# render_scaffold emit a scaffold with no README and no convention file in
# production while every offline test passed, because tests read the source tree
# and production reads the image. Belt to the braces in app/scaffold/__init__.py,
# which refuses to render an incomplete template rather than emitting one.
!backend/app/scaffold/template/**
